*(
    title: Simple Harmonic Motion
    description: Motion whose acceleration points back towards a centre and grows in proportion to the distance from it.
    tags: mechanics, simple harmonic motion, oscillation, amplitude, period, extension 2, stub
    lesson
)

@include(src: ../preface.part.chalk)

scene{
    One condition on the acceleration — proportional to the displacement from a fixed point, and directed back towards it — is enough to determine the motion completely. Everything oscillates the same way under it, whatever the physical cause.

    Written out here: the defining equation, its sine and cosine solutions and why either can be written as the other with a phase shift, amplitude, period and frequency read off the constants, the velocity as a function of displacement, and identifying the centre of motion when the equation arrives shifted away from the origin.
}
